{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions","id":1513165,"title":"Koldunism questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-28T23:10:33-07:00","id":1513165,"title":"Koldunism questions","content":"So i read up a bit on koldunism and immediately some things went through my head that i kinda cant answer myself for sure.<br /> <br /> in general, it may just seem to me this way but koldunism seems pretty weak compared to other blood sorceries, i mean sure it has some nice spells but to me it seems that regular thaumaturgy offers not only way more variation in powery you can wield but wields them much stronger too.<br /> <br /> As example, path of the earth requires people standing on actual soil, making this power quite useless in city areas, buildings, caves or basicly most areas modern day vampires are around. it does make sense lorewise but Thaumaturgy or Dur an ki dont have such restrictions they just conjure up their powers anywhere if i am not mistaken.<br /> And not only is there a physical restrictions but the way i read the lore you are supposed to be one with the spirits of the land, meaning the koldun cant use koldunism outside his own domain?<br /> <br /> Next it seems to affect the caster itself. If i read on biting gale it says EVERYONE caught in the storm suffers the effects, which should include the koldun himself as he is the center of the storm no?<br /> <br /> Also fire....can that wind extinguish fire or would it actually spread it as wind often likes to do...<br /> <br /> Damagewise i am also a bit confused, cause 1 point of bashing damage per turn seems ignorable. You can soak it normally so i guess most mortals can soak it with ease (does armor count?) and for vampires the damage is halved though i am not sure if 1 isnt the minimum damage so vampires take that too or if it means vampires are effectively immune to the damage.<br /> <br /> And then there is the question of what use the -2 dexterity and halved movement speed is - halved movement speed seems to mean only the speed of moving towards the koldun, or would it mean halved attack speed as well so you only get 1 action per 2 turns instead of every turn making it kinda anti celerity?<br /> <br /> As in usage - the koldun cant take any non reflexive action while casting biting gale so he himself wouldnt be able to take any advantage of the enemies slowed state, and allies he might have, are affected by it as well making it rather useless?<br /> <br /> I could imagine a nice kombo of winds of lethargy which is a one cast and effect lasts for success/turns, grasping earth for rooting the enemy and then biting gale to maximise the bashing damage done to the target from the chilling winds but...again 1 bashing damage is kinda ignorable.<br /> <br /> - does it add to other damage sources that turn? Say suffer an attack dealing 3 bashing damage for a total of 4 to soak or is it, as dseperate source, 3 bashing damage to soak and then you get the full pool again to soak the 1 from the wind?<br /> <br /> The whisper in the wind power also seems weird, as you can use the wind, with a delay and your target required to be &quot;reachable&quot; by the wind while other sources can give you outright telepathy.<br /> <br /> meanwhile for direct comparrison, you can use way of the earth level 2 power to gain 2 dots of stamina, but with thaumaturgy level 1 in elemental strength you get 3 dots AND can distribute them between strength and stamina as you please. So that level 1 power is clearly stronger than the other level 2 power?<br /> <br /> Finally its more epxensive as well...thaumaturgy is an in clan discipline, koldunism is always out of clan...<br /> <br /> I dont know maybe im reading this wrong but it sure seems like koldunism is pretty weak compared to other blood sorceries. Having regional restrictions, physical restrictions, affecting the caster, being more expensive and for that is being outright weaker on top with less diversity. Or am i just mistaken and dont grasp the true power of Kolduns, that id love to have explained to me XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 05-29-2023, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T23:47:02-07:00","id":1513167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions#post1513165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As example, path of the earth requires people standing on actual soil, making this power quite useless in city areas, buildings, caves or basicly most areas modern day vampires are around. it does make sense lorewise but Thaumaturgy or Dur an ki dont have such restrictions they just conjure up their powers anywhere if i am not mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends of the Path or Way, Green Path and Nepune Might have iirc simialr limitations, while Way of the Spirit and Way of Sorrows don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions#post1513165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">meanwhile for direct comparrison, you can use way of the earth level 2 power to gain 2 dots of stamina, but with thaumaturgy level 1 in elemental strength you get 3 dots AND can distribute them between strength and stamina as you please. So that level 1 power is clearly stronger than the other level 2 power?</div> </div> </div> </div>The big difference here is duration, the Endurance of Stone last for a scene, Elemental Strength only for a number of turns equal to the success you rolled, which makes it much harder to use in actual game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions#post1513165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then there is the question of what use the -2 dexterity and halved movement speed is - halved movement speed seems to mean only the speed of moving towards the koldun, or would it mean halved attack speed as well so you only get 1 action per 2 turns instead of every turn making it kinda anti celerity?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was anti celerity it was written there. The power might be kind of weak, but it is only a second level power, Thaumaturgic Path have also often some powers that are either weak or super circumstantial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions#post1513165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know maybe im reading this wrong but it sure seems like koldunism is pretty weak compared to other blood sorceries. Or am i just mistaken and dont grasp the true power of Kolduns, that id love to have explained to me XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Imo the Koldunic Ways tend to be stronger, than Thaumaturgic Path with a similar theme (I mean the second level power of the Way of Fire is potentally better than the entire Lure of Flames Path), but with Thaumaturgy you have of course way more options, and some of the other path are pretty strong.<br /> Koldunic Scorcery is thematically more limited, and probably more suited for the Dark Ages and NPCs than for modern Nights and Player Characters.<br /> But a big advantage of Koludns is the Way of the Spirit, that lets them use their powers from a distance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T00:07:09-07:00","id":1513170,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification so far. Raises another qustion though - can you use &quot;combust&quot; - way of fire level 2 on a distance, because it &quot;can be dodged&quot; but how would one dodge it if they arent even aware of an attack?<br /> <br /> Also since you can use this once per turn, wouldnt that mean that basicly a Koldun with way of spirit 3+ and level 2 way of fire is the ultimate vampire assasin as he could obliterate entire coteries inside building A while chilling savely hidden on the 50th floor of the building 5 blocks away?<br /> <br /> and since you can use way of spirit during the day (if you go to rest while having it active)....5 dots for a 5 mile radius in way of spirit + combust, you could obliterate most of your enemies while they are in torpor oO which would then raise the question why kolduns just dont do so and basicly anhiliate the camarilla by themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T03:45:43-07:00","id":1513184,"title":"","content":"Upon further reseach i can see some serious dice stacking though.<br /> <br /> If you play a Grimaldi with the merit revenant disciplines, max fortitude to 5, then take way of earth and buff yourself with the level 2, max your stamina to 5, then occult to 5, you get a total of 17 dice to roll on any way of earth sorcery. which, the level 1 already could potentially deal 17 lethal damage...(17 dice, diff 4)<br /> <br /> - 5 dice from the fortitude passive bonus, 5 from stamina, 5 from occult 2 from the buff endurance of stone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T09:16:01-07:00","id":1513200,"title":"","content":"It's also worth pointing out that Way of Spirit, RAW, often gets treated as a blanket anti-Obfuscate, without contested rolls or anything IIRC.<br /> <br /> And yes, Way of Fire 2 + Way of Spirit As-Much-As-Possible has always been one of my favourite combinations when it comes to the Ways. I regard it less as an assassin and more as a defender, however: stick that Koldun in some kind of fortification, have them sweeping their domain with Way of Spirit every night, immolate anything that they think doesn't belong. It does work for assassination too, but that's much more exposed, and in a supernatural world you have to count on other people being able to work out your MO and come up with fantastic countermeasures, while you lack the defences you would have in your home territory.<br /> <br /> And since that point hasn't been addressed from what I can see, I'll touch on your concerns about the regional limitations of Koldunism. The answer is that it's not generally a limitation. IIRC &quot;modern&quot; Koldunism tended to include a lot of powers and rituals that specialized in strengthening your Domain (like animating the objects in your home, for example), which made sense because the Tzimisce are highly territorial and uniquely bound to their homeland. Meanwhile, the version of Koldunism that they came up with for DA:V20 doesn't use the basic elemental Ways, but instead has Paths called &quot;Kraina&quot; that are tied to specific regions; you can use them anywhere, but if you use a Kraina in the associated territory then it doesn't cost Blood IIRC.<br /> <br /> It is true that Koldunism is somewhat limited in comparison to the flexibility of Thaumaturgy, but you can open up a lot of doors with rituals, and by exploring the implications of Koldunism being a spiritual kind of Blood Sorcery. And the modern Ways come with undeniable raw power to make up for their limited options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T10:12:45-07:00","id":1513206,"title":"","content":"I think using any power through Way Of Spirit line of sight is completely broke and probably not what people intended, or at least they didn't intend it with WoF2, since that one explicitly comes from your eyes. Way of spirit is still great and yeah it should beat Obfuscate given the ranges involved. <br /> <br /> <br /> Way of Air's flight power is incredible. <br /> Way of Fire 2 is one of the best attack magics in the game. Also you look like a boss doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T12:08:19-07:00","id":1513218,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers and clarifications =)<br /> <br /> Yes flight is neat, i guess id use it mainly to escape to my haven if things go sour sadly it doesnt work inside buildings which would be the biggest problem for an escape. I mean for normal transport its a bit unneccesary when you have cars or helicopters<br /> <br /> that said while combust comes form your eyes what it does is heat the air around the victim so it seems your eyes arent neccesary, sight is, which path of spirit kinda provides.<br /> <br /> But to the above statement, i think its usable for assasination - if you bring it to 5 dots you have a 5 mile radius for the power, which, inside cities that are the standard setting for the game, theres a high chance many of your biggest enemies are within 5 miles from your own haven and thus you could assasinate them from the savety of your home, even during the day apparently","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T16:02:03-07:00","id":1513247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513218#post1513218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But to the above statement, i think its usable for assasination - if you bring it to 5 dots you have a 5 mile radius for the power, which, inside cities that are the standard setting for the game, theres a high chance many of your biggest enemies are within 5 miles from your own haven and thus you could assasinate them from the savety of your home, even during the day apparently</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I am not at all trying to deny that it is usable as an assassination power. My comments were more meant to convey that my first thought about that combination was defending domain rather than active assassination. I did also misunderstand you a bit and assume you meant someone acting as an assassin in a 'professional' context, where they are taking jobs and going out after targets, rather than simply targeting neighbouring rivals. In that context, we're 100% in agreement.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Koldun with Way of Spirit/Genius Loci, the range of that power very effectively becomes the natural border of the territory you could expect them to claim as their domain, precisely because it is such a powerful form of influence. Every other being within that area can effectively give up on having much in the way of secrets during the night, and are at constant risk of magical retaliation.<br /> <br /> Way of Spirit really is too much, as much as I love it, and I do feel the need to add some house rules to make it a bit more balanced, though I love the casting-at-distance too much to touch that, haha.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T20:57:31-07:00","id":1513261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513247#post1513247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Way of Spirit really is too much, as much as I love it, and I do feel the need to add some house rules to make it a bit more balanced, though I love the casting-at-distance too much to touch that, haha.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>i understand that XD i guess the simplest way would be to reduce the distance it can be used at. 5 miles is fine for a medieval context thats basicly one village and surrounding fields and one small village or town as domain is fine. In the modern day with cities of millions, 5 miles radius is just insane. Maybe the gauntlet or the sleepers paradigm shift towards reason or other supernatural shenannigans like ravnos waking up changed, for whatever reason, the difficulty of way of spirit, limiting its range to something one would reasonably claim as domain in a metropolitan area.<br /> <br /> And since lorewise as i understand koldunism actually comes from demons, and kolduns and molochim banded together to defeat kuppala, i can see the very act of rebinding kuppala having resulted in a loss of power for kolduns that might manifest in way of spirit being less effective (or being removed alltogether)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T23:46:48-07:00","id":1513266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513261#post1513261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And since lorewise as i understand koldunism actually comes from demons</div> </div> </div> </div>This was always a bit of a question<br /> Depending the source, really<br /> <br /> In essence, Koldunic Sorcery requiring the service of the spirits of nature rather than memorized rites and rituals<br /> The prime example is <b>Kupala's Night</b>\u200b<br /> The pagan ways are the old ways of the Earth, and sometimes Christians fear them with good reason. Just as there is light in the world, there is darkness, and during the festival of Kupala's Night, the force of darkness is undeniably strong. Tzimisce mystics and feudal lords often travel to the knezates of other respected rulers at this time, setting aside their feuds long enough to commune with the ancient spirits<br /> Mortal pagans practice Kupala's Night on June 22nd. They also revere Kupala as a benevolent god.Tzimisce, of course, know both suppositions for the lies they are. The true rituals of Kupala's Night are performed on a different night each year. Only Tzimisce astrologers can discern the most efficacious day for performing the violent ceremony. The veil between the land offlesh and the realm ofspirit is easierto rend on this night, and those who revere the old ways can see the very taint of the earth. Horrible apparitions infect the land, and where the soil has been corrupted, the hideousforms of the kupala can be seen by moonlight. They thrash and gibber, contorting their bodies into impossible displays of physiological degeneration.<br /> The land and the ruler are one, and so the Transylvanian Tzimisce show their reverence for the land by sharing their blood with each other and the earth. With the assistance of mystics, participants enact an ancient rite involving the sharing of blood, A silver cup containing the vitae of all in the ceremony is passed around to be consumed and the last few drops are poured on the ground. This not only demonstrates their alliance, but it also fortifies them for the task at hand.<br /> The screams of the kupala stop as terror seizes the spirits.<br /> Then the slaying begins.<br /> Vengeful Tzimisce distend their bodies and sharpen bloody claws. The spirits cry for mercy, yet none is given. Freely killing the maddening evil in the soil, the Fiends purify the land in obeisance to their ancient pact to protect it. Their fervor escalates into all-consuming frenzy much too often, and nothing in the vicinity is safe.<br /> By dawn, the madness fades and the evil of Kupala is weakened once again.<br /> Hospitality is extended to guests who assisted in the reaving the following night. The truce between collaborators lasts long enough for travelers to return to their fiefdoms. in a week or two, the fierce fighting for control of the land renews, but by then, the greatest of the clan's enemies has been grievously wounded.<br /> <br /> The Tzimsice actually enter the Umbra and technically hunt down Banes and other nasties on their domain, putting the Werewolves to shame<br /> <br /> (On Kupala's Night, the Gauntlet in areas infected by the kupala drops to 2. Tzimisce koldun enact a Level Five Thaumaturgy or Koldunic Sorcery (see Libellus Sanguinis 1 : Masters of the State] ritual allowing the Tzimisce to enter the Penumbra and battle the spirits.)<br /> <br /> Several rituals deal with the spirits<br /> <br /> <b>Lv1.<br /> Hospitality</b>: The Koldun awakens the spirits in an area attuned to him, like his Haven, animating the objects and granting them limited sentience. The objects speak if spoken to and sometimes even when the Koldun does not command, though always with deference and fear. (Players Guide to High Clans)<br /> <br /> <b>Lv2.<br /> Service for Souls: </b>The Koldun summons the spirits of nature and mystically &quot;ghouls&quot; them by offering them his blood. The bound spirits remain with him until their task is fulfilled. (Sins of the Blood)<br /> <br /> <b>Withering Agony:</b> The Koldun draws the spirit from a sick tree out and puts it into another body. The now infected creature suffers from physical debilitations. (Sins of the Blood)<br /> <br /> <b>Lv3.<br /> Raze the L\u00e9lek: </b>The Koldun destroy a physical object by rending away its inhabiting spirit. (L\u00e9lek means Soul in Hungarian) (Sins of the Blood)<br /> <b>Conjure Spirit: </b>The Koldun summons a greater nature spirit to negotiate the task the spirit shall do for him. Most Spirits take offerings and oblations in blood, but others are more picky. (Players Guide to High Clans)<br /> <br /> <b>Lv4.</b><br /> <b>Ties that Bind</b>: The Koldun spills blood on the earth before him. Then, he ritually eats the blood-soaked earth to reconnect with the land, gaining a greater connection to its spirits and more power for his sorceries. (Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy)<br /> <br /> <b>Merging of the Spirit: </b>The Koldun sends a nature spirit to inhabit the body of one of his Ghouls by feeding him extra blood intended to attract the spirits. A ghouls body can take at least three spirits before it warps into something inhumane. (Sins of the Blood)<br /> <br /> <b>Lv5<br /> Elemental Servitor: </b>The Koldun summons a spirit to assume corporeal form to fight for his summoner. (Sins of the Blood)<br /> <br /> <b>Conjure Demon: </b>The Koldun summons one of the spawns of Kupala. The Koldun may barter with the demon for favours. (Players Guide to High Clans)<br /> <br /> <b>Nemesis of the Living Earth:</b> Beginning a long malediction lasting from midnight to sunrise, a koldun may name a target as an enemy of nature. If successful, the victim finds that the elements turn against it to harm it. (Players Guide to High Clans)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lv6.</b><br /> <b>Embracing the Demon: </b>The Koldun may summon a demon into the corpse of a childe-vessel previously put under the blood bond. A demon bound in such a way will serve the Koldun faithfully. (Sins of the Blood)<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Hound: </b>The Koldun builds a fire out of dried herbs and wood from lightning struck trees. Sacrificing a puppy and vitae to the Slavic storm god Perun in the flames, the Koldun creates a storm that can be pointed to any person in the world, as long as the Koldun is in possession of a piece of their body (like hair). The storm will find the target even if it is at the other end of the world. (Lair of the Hidden)<br /> <br /> As you can see there is a very clear distinction of Demons/Banes (kupalas) and nature spirits when it comes to Koldunic Sorcery - actually the rituals are negotiations, not brute force, and only at the very end you start to deal with &quot;demons&quot; (or Banes)<br /> The deals and pacts between spirits of Nature are not something new in WoD when it comes to the undead<br /> The werewolves of the west rarely care to differentiate between a Kuei-jin and a vampire, the Hengeyokai are often forced into contact with them. The Beast Courts keep up formal, if not warm, relations with the Kuei-jin; although these walking corpses are certainly vile, they do have their purpose under Heaven<br /> The Nushi are similar to Garou's Totem, but can be shared by members of a Wu (Pack/Coterie) of Kuei-Jin (or other oriental Shen.)<br /> More so, the editions can't really agree the Tzimsice hace Koldunic Sorcery or not before the Eldest made some deals with Kupala (and handed the furry behind of the Shadow Lords to them)<br /> Clanbook Tzimisce Revised goes to the point it states they indeed had Koldunic sorcery but after the pacts with Kupala (and actually it is NOT the curse of Caine, but the side effect of this pact and/or Koldunism) the Tzimisce are tied to their land) it became stronger<br /> <br /> Here is a funny Comparison!<br /> <b>Gaia's Vengeance (Rank 5 Gift)</b><br /> The Garou calls to the spirits of the surrounding forest to attack intruders. The terrain responds as best it can: Rocks roll and smash, vines trip, and water sucks victims under. An avatar of Gaia herself teaches this Gift.<br /> <b>System: </b>The player spends one Gnosis point and one Rage point then rolls Charisma + Primal-Urge (difficulty of the local Gauntlet). The exact effects depend on the terrain and are left to the Storyteller.<br /> \u200b<br /> <b>Gaia's Vengeance</b>\u200b, the Rank 5 Gift of the Garou and <b>Nemesis of the Living Earth,</b> the level 5 Koldunic Ritual... is basically the same<br /> <br /> Just immagine the sheer terror and confusion of a Garou who bang his furry chest, me Champion of Gaia, you Leech, you hollyfukingshitwhatareyoudoing??? as the Koldun turns the very nature against him and Nature spirits <i>actually vouch for him</i>, yeah, the undead dude is okay, we have a working relationship and he keeps the area clean of the banes and nasty spirits...<br /> These things puts several things in perspective \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-30-2023, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T00:05:26-07:00","id":1513269,"title":"","content":"Okkkkaaay, so I landed in an unaproved post... again<br /> I wonder when this will be fixed, because oh man, it 