,{"date":"2023-05-30T03:16:59-07:00","id":1513276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just immagine the sheer terror and confusion of a Garou who bang his furry chest, me Champion of Gaia, you Leech, you hollyfukingshitwhatareyoudoing??? as the Koldun turns the very nature against him and Nature spirits <i>actually vouch for him</i>, yeah, the undead dude is okay, we have a working relationship and he keeps the area clean of the banes and nasty spirits...<br /> These things puts several things in perspective \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>And that's before realizing koldunes straight up have the ability to learns a form of spirit gifts if you look into koldunic Rites in the dark ages book of secrets.<br /> <br /> European Tzimisce should be an existential crisis to any werewolves that come across them. Especially since shame around the war of rage is still fresh in the garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T04:09:05-07:00","id":1513278,"title":"","content":"Yeah, thats a fun little part too<br /> Toss the fact in to the mix, Grandfather Thunder himself the mighty Incarna of the Shadowlords, not some little natrue spirit or soemthing took the whole Danislav Ravenant family under its dark wings, to the point they had Family Disciplines: Auspex, Protean, Vicissitude... AND could learn Shadow Lords Gifts up to Level 3 as an out-of-clan Discipline?<br /> Any Garou who encounter an European Tzimisce probbaly toss its arms in the air with a rolling eyes, okay, I'm done... I need some strong drink now, where is that Fianna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T05:08:17-07:00","id":1513281,"title":"","content":"Thank you for this amazing summary. I thought demons because of Kuppala and that he may have tainted the spirits of nature to do his bidding. Afaik after Kuppala almost awoke an the combined might of Kolduns and Baali (Molochim) and the Baali can now learn koldunic sorcery from them (in the Tal Mahe Ra at least)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T05:12:19-07:00","id":1513282,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Shadeprowler;n1513269]Okkkkaaay, so I landed in an unaproved post... again<br /> (and actually it is NOT the curse of Caine, but the side effect of this pact and/or Koldunism) the Tzimisce are tied to their land) it became stronger<br /> <br /> I wanted to add here, what would then be their curse of caine, it is not fleshcrafting as i udnerstand it, depending on the source that was added way later? <br /> <br /> Thank you for this amazing summary. I thought demons because of Kuppala and that he may have tainted the spirits of nature to do his bidding. Afaik after Kuppala almost awoke an the combined might of Kolduns and Baali (Molochim) and the Baali can now learn koldunic sorcery from them (in the Tal Mahe Ra at least)<br /> and actually it is NOT the curse of Caine, but the side effect of this pact and/or Koldunism) the Tzimisce are tied to their land\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T06:16:54-07:00","id":1513284,"title":"","content":"Their weakness is basically from where do you want to aproach the quetion<br /> The Clan Curse of the Tzimisce is their need to rest in &quot;native soil&quot; \u2013 earth from a place important to them when they were mortal. - this is the default, so to speak, Caine handed out the curse, nice and simple<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Erciyes Fragments state: &quot;Behold, my most loveless childe, who fed upon his brother's pain. Let him know equal torment in any domain but its own&quot;<br /> <br /> Both Erciyes Fragments and Book of Nod point at Caine who handed out the Curse... but important to note, not to the whole Clan. At the moment not many were around to be a Clan, per se, the Antediluvian was cursed. Fro mthem &quot;spread&quot; so to speak with various factors.<br /> <br /> Revalations of the Dark Mother introduces the Bahari myths witch tell that the Eldest was cursed by Lilith along with Set and the Brujah Antediluvian, when they slaughtered Lilith's children<br /> <br /> Clanbook: Followers of Set Revised reveals, the Followers of Set believe that the Tzimisce are the creations of Geb, who placed their lineage under the dominion of Scorpio. The Earth-God gave them the dominion over flesh, but tied them to the soil of their homeland in exchange<br /> <br /> In Clanbook: Tzimsice Revised, some of he Clan claims that the Eldest left the First City long before the Deluge, however, and Caine cursed them <i>in absentia</i>, for dealing with the demon Kupala under the Carpathians and their inhospitality to their brethren following the Deluge.<br /> But the same book also tells us, the Koldun believe the weakness is a debt to the land-spirits of their native domains, whose power affects all that falls under the shadow of the Carpathians and had nothing to do with Caine's cursing of the other Antediluvians<br /> Again, the clanbook also gives some reinforcement ot the Kupala-theory; the soil-bound entity Kupala as well their territorial nature, became the clan\u2019s anathema when the curse forced them to sleep upon their native soil for true rest. Some Tzimisce are so attuned to it that they can only rest in the soil touched by Kupala...<br /> Also also the Clanbook reveals Agoraphobia is common among the more sensitive members of the Clan, as their connection to the earth makes them uncomfortable in open spaces - a bit of a &quot;side curse&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bSome more arcane researchers state that Vicissitude's tendency to fluctuate creates the need of a stabilizer in order for the Tzimisce to retain his shape, which is supplied via the sympathetic connection of native soil - at least according Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand<br /> <br /> The 2002 Dark Ages: Vampire Rulebook tells us how the Voivodes of old existed in symbiosis with the spirits, offering blood sacrifices to renew the earth, infusing the land with his essence in exchange for strength and shelter<br /> <br /> Finally in V5 the Tzimisce recieved hte Bane <b>Grounded </b>(Each Tzimisce must choose a specific charge \u2014 a physical domain, a group of people, an organization, or even something more esoteric \u2014 but clearly defined and limited. The Kindred must spend their daysleep surrounded by their chosen charge. Historically this has often meant slumbering in the soil of their land, but it can also mean being surrounded by that which they tonight rule: a certain kind of people, a building deeply tied to their obsession, a local counterculture faction, or other, more outlandish elements. If they do not, they sustain aggravated Willpower damage equal to their Bane Severity upon waking the following night) and the Compulsion <b>Covetousness </b>(when a Tzimisce suffers a Compulsion, the Kindred becomes obsessed with possessing something in the scene, desiring to add it to their proverbial hoard. This can be anything from an object to a piece of property to an actual person. Any action not taken toward this purpose incurs a two-dice penalty. The Compulsion persists until ownership is established (the Storyteller decides what constitutes ownership in the case of a non-object) or the object of desire becomes unattainable.)<br /> <br /> When it comes to a Clan's curse/weaknesess it is important to note, Caine rarely if ever went to such a length to curse the whole bloodline of the Antediluvian<br /> Well of course if you take account the several - tons of - materials over the decades<br /> Originally only Cappadocius looked like a coprse, thank to his botched Embrace and the fact Wraith tried to hold him back and he lost much of it made Sargon Sargon and only remembered, he is from Cappadocia, Caine in this case not cursed the Antediluvian, but his descendants to punish him - or as an alternate, nobody cursed the Cappadocians, the Wraiths were so pissed at Cappadocius, tormented his descendants BUT not the Giovanni, as they planned to use them as the tools of their revenge<br /> The Ventrue dispute that they are cursed at all and that their taste is simply rarefied to the point of exclusivity, something the lesser Clans cannot understand, not to mention their &quot;weakness&quot; is mutable; if a given mortal demographic dies out, another fills it niche; as the Ventrue Andrew Seneca and Democritus demonstrate - how nice from a &quot;Curse&quot;, reducing itself in to minor inconvinience<br /> The Malkavians in this regard is starange, because either Malkav never was sane to begn with... or later became insine. Player Guide to the Low clans tell the story (theory) of the curse is that Malkav was a notorious liar and his lies nearly caused the death of Zillah. Caine, enraged, cursed Malkav with telling an infinite number of &quot;truths&quot; thereafter. The Followers of Se say that the Malkavians are the creation of Isis, under the influence of the zodiac sign of Cancer, who tried to grant supreme wisdom to their founder, and instead shattered his mind and all his descendants likewise.<br /> Interestingly, this a bit similar to the story, how Lilith whispered a secret in Malkavs ears and the wight of it shattered his mind (and Malakai, his twin sister's mind)<br /> Their Clanbook claim that Caine had no hand in cursing the Clan, and that their madness is a result of the insight that rushed through Malkav when he drank deeply from the blood of the Second Generation. In any cases, most of the Malkavians are not sane to begin with, but the MAdnes Network or Malkav's tainted blood drove them mad...<br /> The Assamites themselves claim that Haqim was never cursed by Caine and that the weakness of his descendants stem from his monomaniacal fixation on one focus or passion or duty to the exclusion of all else. This defining trait carried itself through the Blood, marking his lines with that aspect of his personality. More so, it is basically confirmed, the craving for vitae and Diablerie was imposed by the Baali . In 636 CE the Baali, with the aid of the demonic Decani, cursed the Assamite filling them with a murderous hunger for Cainite vitae, ruining their reputation among the other Clans and transforming the ritualistic Amaranth of a guilty culprit into the desire to consume. Additionally, all Assamites succumb to the &quot;Darkening&quot; (except Al-Ashrad for unknown reasons), which turns their skin darker with each passing year, until they have the complexion of obsidian - a weakness nobody actually know where the hell came from (and no one calls it a weakness, nor a curse to be honest), and no sources pinpoints the &quot;Darkening&quot; on one source, no mention of Caine, Lilith, anyone... they are just... Darken. \u200b<br /> <br /> Sorry, wandered off topic, to answer your question, IF the Clan weakness is the result of the Spirits and ties to the earth, then the &quot;og.&quot; Tzimisce Curse was probably something close to the V5 variant - IF there was a cruse at all<br /> Really this is just theory craft, ultimately is up to you and your storyteller <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-30-2023, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T08:25:06-07:00","id":1513293,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> has done an excellent job of summing up the connection between Koldun and the spirits of nature. However, I would like to complicate that account a bit. Specifically, the idea that Koldunic Sorcery should make Garou and other Fera rethink their opinions of Cainites due to the connection between Koldun and the land. It's not something that comes up too often, but some sources do describe Tzimisce sorcery as corrupting the land and the spirits under its influence:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Player's Guide to the High Clans, p.185</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is certain is that Koldunic Sorcery is not gentle or kind to the earth, any more than the Fiends are gentle to the beasts and men who walk upon the earth. Just as the Tzimisce fleshcraft servants to tend their masters better, so too do koldun warp the land and its nature to serve their own ends. Such gross violations of the natural order offend the Lupines, but the Tzimisce have endured too long to flinch from the ire of cringing dogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This quote doesn't quite make the same explicit point, but it does get across that even the Koldunic Sorcery practiced before the Anarch Revolt and the adoption of the Ways was tainted to some extent:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tome of Secrets, p.45</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzimisce balk at the idea of serving any beings, let alone demons. Yet, something infernal exists in the kraina. Koldunic Sorcery is the raw power of the earth, but also contains the spite and discord of demons \u2014 the most infamous being Kupala. Cursed blood should not mix with nature, yet this is the fundament of the koldun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also important to not that a common feature of the Koldunic rituals listed above frequently include the act of feeding vitae to the spirits you are bargaining with. If you buy into the idea that the Kindred condition is a Curse of some kind, then Koldunism as practiced by the Tzimisce seems to at least partially involve spreading that Curse to the spirit world. And the local Lupines are *not* going to look favourably on that.<br /> <br /> Part of why I spoke earlier about exploring the &quot;implications&quot; of the spiritual nature of Koldunism is that the source material doesn't really go into much detail on the matter. All of those rituals Shadeprowler listed above that involve bargaining with spirits, and there is no official discussion of how Koldun interact with or influence the wider Umbra, beyond the Kupala's Night ritual mentioned above that allows the Tzimisce to destroy the lesser kupala spirits.<br /> <br /> In my personal headcanon, I have tended to view the long-term practice of Koldunism in a region as having a corrupting influence on the local spirits that deal with the Koldun, becoming tainted by the dark power of the blood mage's vitae. While whether or not the Curse of vampirism is actually Wyrmish, I imagine that the effects definitely ping the Wyrm-sense of Garou in the same way that most Kindred do. In particular, the spirits under the Koldun's influence become &quot;bloodthirsty,&quot; looking for opportunities to draw blood or injure people, and the Umbral environment itself becomes bloodier and more predatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T09:05:52-07:00","id":1513295,"title":"","content":"Those are excelent points <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\">Kharnov</a> </b>pointed out<br /> And yes, - even if we don't factor Vicissitude as a spiritual disease from the Dark Umbra option - Vitae is probably not that healthy<br /> But from another point of view vitae is a substance blood transforms in to and thus it is full of power, is just a conduit; Chi, Quintessence, etc, hard to translate the Powers of different settings, but I don't think it is necessarily inherently &quot;evil&quot; or spiritually corrosive<br /> Really depends on how deep you want to wander in to this rabit hole <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513293#post1513293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Umbral environment itself becomes bloodier and more predatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Regarding this one... my headcanon in this matter is simple: Vampires are predators<br /> And if anything, Nature is <i>cruel</i><br /> Nature is riddled with suffering and misery. We see as much in a myriad of beautifully made wildlife films, as one animal is eviscerated live by another or desiccated by its environment.<br /> Life in the wild is 'brutal, tough and unforgiving' - in other words \u2018cruel\u2019.<br /> Nature favours efficiency, efficiency favours entropy, entropy implies humaneness. Pointless pain and misery would seem an inefficient use of nature\u2019s resources.<br /> Some people may argue that nature can be cruel because it can cause natural disasters and diseases, while others may argue that nature is beautiful and harmonious. Ultimately, whether nature is cruel or not is a subjective perception and can depend on the context and perspective of the observer.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Queen, also known as the Scarlet Phoenix, is one of the Ministers of Creation, the ruler of the Yang World, but the Beast Courts of the Middle Kingdom, however, identify Gaia as the Emerald Mother, a different being altogether with roughly equal status to the August Personage<br /> <br /> &quot;Green mother Nature, Red of tooth and claw.&quot;<br /> <br /> And this summs her up perfectly<br /> Gaia... Natrue is... well, not nice.<br /> Nautural sellection, survival of the fittest, natural disasters and diseases... extinctions...<br /> I don't think Natrue or the Umbra really &quot;needs&quot; the blood of a Tzimsice to make it deadlier, bloodier or predatory or would deepen these basically natural, brutal traits<br /> But of curse this is how I see it, Vampires are - while &quot;cursed&quot;, undead and ultimately the agents of Stasis (stucked in a moment, like how Weaver froze Luna, never aging, hard to change if ever, and every night reset their bodies to the point of the Embrace) not really the Wyrm - are Predators thus have their own place in the order of things, eg. Nature<br /> <br /> But <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\">Kharnov</a>'s </b>examples are totally right\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T09:41:02-07:00","id":1513299,"title":"","content":"Amazing post once again thank you =) i like theories XD i have a whole youtube channel dedicated to clan Baali - that lore im pretty good with and they offer lots of theories, most o which are not proven and some being crazy. As like, there is a theoy the Baali turned themselves into vampires similiar to the nagaraja, when the first tribe was still a thing and are thus not cainites at all but their founders are all 1st gen, which explains why baali blood can override all others.<br /> Another theory is that there were 13 2nd gen vampires that formed the original coven and created the original Baali, which explains why sometimes there is as many as 6 founders mentioned not the usual 3 - of which 2 are the crone and zillah herself.<br /> <br /> Now if we look across spalts werewolf confirms that nergal is 3rd gen and whats going on with Tremere hints that the Baali are definitely saulots childer (similiar blood to tremere) and may have had a hand in creating the Tremre, with, again potentially, a baali in the circle of 7 (thomas wyncham) not to mention some well known vampires may be baali (petaniquah is kinda confirmed, Ur Shulgi is...well what you want to believe) and Azaneal was listed as 2nd gen vampire, likely lowering his generation when he diablerised whatever he found in Chorazin. (Erashkigal is a rumor explaining his power over the abyss that puts lasombra mystics to shame)<br /> <br /> Back to Kolduns, how united are they? It does seem that &quot;THE&quot; Kolduns at least when i came to putting Kuppala back to sleep seemed very united, and since they are highly respected among the old clan it also seems there is a kind of unity amongst them, yet Kolduns can be sabbath or old clan and even then Tzimisce have this thing of hating each other more than almost anyone else XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T09:53:18-07:00","id":1513300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513295#post1513295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are excelent points <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\">Kharnov</a> </b><br /> <br /> And this summs her up perfectly<br /> <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\">Kharnov</a>'s </b>examples are totally right\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>now i am not that deep into the lore but from what i gather vampires are considered evil and unnatural from any point of view<br /> <br /> first, if you go with the book of nod, they were literally cursed by god / the angels and thus the powers of creation. Second, they are definitely beings that shouldnt exist according to nature, they are dead people walking, and slipping ever further away from the humanity that made them, becoming uncontrollable murderous beasts that more and more enjoy suffering of others. (which some animals do too btw)<br /> <br /> third, they were cursed again by caine...and others...and you can artifially become a vampire by committing quite heinous deeds as seen in the Tremere or Nagaraja (which technicly menas they arent cainites per se as they technicly dont hail from caine)<br /> <br /> afaik all fera regard vampires as wyrm aligned, some more, some less, and most hunters have a hard time seeing a vampire as something they can let live, though certain creeds might accept high humanity vampires.<br /> <br /> for cosmic powers i read somewhere that magick wielded by true mages has a raised difficulty to be cast near vampires as vampires are such static beings that reality hardens around them, which is one explanation why their powers never cause paradox, even blood magic doesnt despite being very versatile and not as bound as other disciplines which would align vampires more with the weaver than the wyrm. similarily vampires are anachronistic barely changing creatures, the older thy are the more out of touch they become, also speaking more for the weaver as they are...wel static. <br /> most vampires arent technicly &quot;evil&quot; or tainted either as they resist the beast - the beast sounds very much wyrm like yet garou seem to have little issues with gangrel who give into their beast more so than others which i kinda dont understnad but ok...^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T11:12:04-07:00","id":1513306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513282#post1513282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought demons because of Kuppala and that he may have tainted the spirits of nature to do his bidding. Afaik after Kuppala almost awoke an the combined might of Kolduns and Baali (Molochim) and the Baali can now learn koldunic sorcery from them (in the Tal Mahe Ra at least)<br /> and actually it is NOT the curse of Caine, but the side effect of this pact and/or Koldunism) the Tzimisce are tied to their land\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit of overlap between Baali lore and koldunism that wasn't present before both ideas were a bit more developed throughout the editions. Koldunism is something that would be far more suited to the Baali than (just) Daimonion, and I will throw in the Lhiannan and Telyavelic Tremere as well. I'm currently not running Vampire but if I do, I would be tempted to assign a common lore background (ie the Baali Children) to those bloodlines and have them all use koldunism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T12:09:00-07:00","id":1513309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513306#post1513306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a bit of overlap between Baali lore and koldunism that wasn't present before both ideas were a bit more developed throughout the editions. Koldunism is something that would be far more suited to the Baali than (just) Daimonion, and I will throw in the Lhiannan and Telyavelic Tremere as well. I'm currently not running Vampire but if I do, I would be tempted to assign a common lore background (ie the Baali Children) to those bloodlines and have them all use koldunism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well lorewise the Baali are the original vampires to use blood sorcery as in, the very first. Lroewise dark thaumaturgy is identical to tremere thaumaturgy for almost all purposes, you can learn thaumaturgy paths using dark thaumaturgy ratings instead, dark thaumaturgy comes with a twist but ultimately all thaumaturgy stems from demons.<br /> <br /> As angels (and thus demons) created creation and its laws (on behalf of god) they apparently made thaumaturgy work (which is why it doesnt invoke paradox unlike true magick that wasnt implemented in reality &quot;source code) and thus demons taught vampires (apparently caine was the first to learn thaumaturgy from lucifer as a pact is hinted at in the book of nod when lilith denied to teach caine how to awaken)<br /> <br /> anyway the baali are the first clan to wield ANY blood sorcery and it was dark thaumaturgy which they may have taught the Tremere who expanded on it without demonic help using their kowledge of hedge sorcery and true magick. (its not too far off that Tremere was guided to sleeping saulot by saulot and/or Baali, and given Saulot spawned 3 very evil vile clans and the salubri and is called saulot the liar in the east and given what he does to tremere himself i think its obvious saulot is not a good guy)<br /> <br /> similarily ur shulgi the true master of dur an ki was Baali (and may still be, thats up for personal liking if the purging from haquim worked or not) and baali at least used to know necromancy (used in the Baali wars) and with Azaneal are masters of obtenebration as well (which uses oblivions powers, which is where the demons are trapped)<br /> <br /> hence, Baali are known to aquire knowledge from demons (Nergali with pacts, Molochim with force) and Kupala is, at the end of the day, another demon (and may not be the only one to know koldunism. I mean the Baali have dagoth in their hands (his...whatever the device that holds an earthbound is called again) and dagoth is earthbound too so...they could also have learned from him<br /> <br /> that said, since Molochim can now learn koldunism through the tal mahe ra (as well as other blood sorceries provided by the Verbena mages) i dont really see a need to give them access to koldunism in other ways, but if you run a dark ages campaign you could do it, i mean the Molochim and Tzimisce worked together before (first and second Baali wars) and clashed in constantinople so...<br /> <br /> that said Baali could always have dark thaumaturgy as out of clan discipline, giving them access to koldunism as well may have, game designer wise, just broken the powerlevel too much. (that aside daimonion is a pretty shit discipline compared to most others and at least its first 2 levels seem to have been designed to be storyteller tools and not for player character hands as youd constantly have to ask the ST about info on other characters that he might have to ask the players blowing yur cover)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T12:34:27-07:00","id":1513313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> vampires are considered evil and unnatural from any point of view </div> </div> </div>I'm firmly of the opinion that something can not exist and be unnatural, they're two exclusive concepts. If it exists, some laws of the universe are enabling its existence. If that were not so, it couldn't exist outside of the human imagination. &quot;Unnatural&quot; is simply a word that means &quot;I don't like that this exists, and I want it to stop existing.&quot; And if we're going with the Abrahamic lore and saying vampirism was created by the almighty god of the WoD you cannot get more natural than that. Vampires are totally natural phenomena of the WoD, and that's because the WoD is innately horrific and fundamentally broken place. A symptom of the disease, rather than a disease in and of themselves, if you will.<br /> (Sure, the books can call them unnatural all they like, but I disagree with them; that's not a thing.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">(This is more of a person interpretation rather than anything I think was intentional by the writers, but I also question the notion that vampires are dead. Like if; a) they're truly dead (they're<i> undead</i>, it's a grey area with them suspended between the states of death (torpor) and life (blush of life). The increased vitality of the highest generations could be taken to suggest that the curse is suppressing vitality, rather than animating a dead thing. Thinbloods didn't die any less than the lower gens, and their vitae should be too weak to animate them to such a degree if it's the curse alone that keeps the body moving) and/or b) that the body<i> is</i> the vampire, rather than the thing <i>inside</i> the body (vitae). You can damage the body to hell and back and it won't make much of a difference, because the body is simply a tool, but if you suck the last drop of vitae out of the heart (or destroy the heart so that it can't contain the heartsblood anymore) then it dies, because the parasite has been removed from the host. In a case where that hypothesis/headcanon is correct, the &quot;walking dead&quot; bit isn't a hurdle because vampires aren't dead.)</span><br /> <br /> Nor is anything vampires do particularly unnatural; drinking blood, theft, murder, desecrating corpses, brainwashing, domesticating other species for your own use, slavery, ruining the world around you for your own benefit, violent fight/flight responses, vicious dominance hierarchies and so forth are all things nature is perfectly happy to invent on its own and if nature has an issue with vampires doing these things, nature is a hypocrite. Vampires just have power unseen in the real world and specifically affect humans, that's all.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm vs Weaver thing is iffy. Overall, they seem far more Weaver aspected more than anything else, but they do lower the Shroud rating with their presence, which maybe suggests something somewhat Wyrm-ish about them if they're causing an entropy effect. Then again, nothing says they can't be tainted by two thirds of the Triat at once.<br /> <br /> And none of this is to suggest that vampires aren't collectively an awful blight on the world, nor that the other splats don't have good reason to consider them evil considering they're actively harmful to them (either because they'll eat you (humans, hunters, changelings, mages) or because they're worsening the corruption of the world that you're trying to survive in/save (wraiths, garou), just to list two of many reasons).<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Also more on topic; regardless of power levels, the main thing Koldunic sorcery has going for it, in my opinion, is how damn cinematic it is. A city facing the wrath of a powerful elder can be plunged into constant darkness under a seemingly eternal thunderstorm, as floods and fires and earthquakes rock the world, animals turn on their owners and go violently insane all over the town for no comprehensible reason, spectres run rampant, people are reported to disappear; sucked into the earth, only to reappear drained of blood, with their faces in a rictus of horror. Horrific visions appear in bodies of water, a cruel voice whispers on the icy winds that appear during what was supposed to be a midsummer heatwave... power be damned, it's great fun. Masquerade shattering fun, but fun, and a great backdrop for a story.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T13:35:14-07:00","id":1513316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513313#post1513313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm firmly of the opinion that something can not exist and be unnatural, they're two exclusive concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nephandi exist and they want to undo creation and all its laws. Mages bend and break the laws of existance and the universe on a very regular basis.<br /> Nature is not the same as existance either in my oppinion, most of the universe as in by far the most of it doesnt carry any life. and not even the laws of nature apply everywhere equally, we actually know that these laws change under certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> that said, the natural way things are supposed to go is - thing dies, rots away, is gone. Something dieing, not rotting and still walking around but without anything that actually uis required for living like say a heartbeat...that is not natural.<br /> <br /> now obviously when existance was created by the angels they somehow made undeath, vampires, blood magic etc. a thing otherwise they would invoke paradox. Obviously demons taught caine blood sorcery so they know all about it, hence that is made manifest in the creation of the world, at the same time it was implemented as curse and meant as punishment which isnt good. it was intended to make caine suffer and he sinned by passing it on.<br /> <br /> if everything existing is natural, then anything that is the anti of its own existance . quiloptic spheres as example, is natural despite its being completly against reality.<br /> <br /> &quot;but I also question the notion that vampires are dead&quot;<br /> - that depends on the definition of life. In chemistry, life is a self sustaining chemical process. Vampires are self sustaining but they arent using any chemical process, they violate any laws of chemistry we know of. In biology, life is growing and replication of cells. vampires kinda do that but again in a way that violates all laws of biology we know of. Philosophicly life is self aware in thes ense of reaction to its surroundings rather than merely being tossed around by them, that would be true for vampires. religiously life is given by god...i guess the curse was given by god so...spiritually life has a soul - that is NOT true for vampires (anymore) but i guess the common definition if life is that it is, well alife...with heartbeat and digestion and can die. none of which are true for vampires who violate all of these things.<br /> <br /> in your definition the dead would be alife (as in wraiths and such) and i guess they would beg to differ here. Undead means that - you arent quite dead but you definitely arent alife. That would be unliving and yes that IS a difference, an important one.Unliving creatures never died and never were brought to the brink of death, they never stopped living, they for whatever reason decayed to a death like state, they dont age anymore, they dont need sustainance from food but they still can die under certain conditions usually removing the item that made them unliving. Mummies in WoD would be unliving. Vampires are undead as they actually did die at the embrace and were forced back by vitae. ghouls are unliving to an extent.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nor is anything vampires do particularly unnatural&quot;<br /> how about violating natural laws like thermodynamics, entropy, gravity...or not aging. even species that are technicly immortal like certain jellyfish DO AGE. they just dont die to it as they can rebirth themselves reverting back to a fetal like state and restarting from there. vampire dont age, there is no process of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot; Vampires just have power unseen in the real world&quot;<br /> in WoD the &quot;real world&quot; is quite the stretch. what is that? the Umbra is in many ways more real, the spirit realms, the abyss...thats very real and all of these very real worlds have being with insanely higher powerlevels. indeed in WoD vampires are about the weakest supernatural creatures in existance. btw the &quot;real world&quot; as in earth is inhabited by mages who are about the most powerfull creatures in the cosmos (depending on their arete rating. i mean exemplars can do shit that not even god could.) and then there is the exalted....what about fae? demons...are they counted here or there? or both? Garou are a bit...well. garou are a lot more powerfull than most vampires. then again once a vampire becomes an elder they just get more powerfull than shapechangers by sheer experience.<br /> <br /> to wyrm - i still go by vampires arent entropic. they dont degenerate, they dont decay. they stand perfectly still (kinda) which is a weaver thing. that said they do tend to cause taint and entropy arround them, in special if they give into their beast. their mere presence may cause entropy in their surroundings (certain vampiric flaws make plants and small life forms literally die from your presence alone)<br /> <br /> overall vampires per se tend to be evil from almost any point of philosophy. but not all vampires are evil. But age also has the tendency to corrupt, as has power and vampires gain both over time, making it less and less likely to be good the older you become.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Also more on topic; regardless of power levels, the main thing Koldunic sorcery has going for it, in my opinion, is how damn cinematic it is&quot;<br /> <br /> well yes...but...other disciplines...take thaumaturgy.can do very similiar things. brujah can punch through a concrete skyscraper while running up its walls. and the true ones can time travel oO<br /> meanwhile ventrue can tank artillery fire, and baali can walk through lava unharmed. not sure how cinematic you would call necromancy with its minions XD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T13:35:18-07:00","id":1513317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513295#post1513295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, - even if we don't factor Vicissitude as a spiritual disease from the Dark Umbra option - Vitae is probably not that healthy<br /> But from another point of view vitae is a substance blood transforms in to and thus it is full of power, is just a conduit; Chi, Quintessence, etc, hard to translate the Powers of different settings, but I don't think it is necessarily inherently &quot;evil&quot; or spiritually corrosive<br /> Really depends on how deep you want to wander in to this rabit hole <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding this one... my headcanon in this matter is simple: Vampires are predators<br /> And if anything, Nature is <i>cruel</i><br /> Nature is riddled with suffering and misery. We see as much in a myriad of beautifully made wildlife films, as one animal is eviscerated live by another or desiccated by its environment.<br /> Life in the wild is 'brutal, tough and unforgiving' - in other words \u2018cruel\u2019.<br /> Nature favours efficiency, efficiency favours entropy, entropy implies humaneness. Pointless pain and misery would seem an inefficient use of nature\u2019s resources.<br /> Some people may argue that nature can be cruel because it can cause natural disasters and diseases, while others may argue that nature is beautiful and harmonious. Ultimately, whether nature is cruel or not is a subjective perception and can depend on the context and perspective of the observer.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Queen, also known as the Scarlet Phoenix, is one of the Ministers of Creation, the ruler of the Yang World, but the Beast Courts of the Middle Kingdom, however, identify Gaia as the Emerald Mother, a different being altogether with roughly equal status to the August Personage<br /> <br /> &quot;Green mother Nature, Red of tooth and claw.&quot;<br /> <br /> And this summs her up perfectly<br /> Gaia... Natrue is... well, not nice.<br /> Nautural sellection, survival of the fittest, natural disasters and diseases... extinctions...<br /> I don't think Natrue or the Umbra really &quot;needs&quot; the blood of a Tzimsice to make it deadlier, bloodier or predatory or would deepen these basically natural, brutal traits<br /> But of curse this is how I see it, Vampires are - while &quot;cursed&quot;, undead and ultimately the agents of Stasis (stucked in a moment, like how Weaver froze Luna, never aging, hard to change if ever, and every night reset their bodies to the point of the Embrace) not really the Wyrm - are Predators thus have their own place in the order of things, eg. Nature</div> </div> </div> </div>I was only sharing my own headcanon as an example when it came to the effects of Koldunism on the Umbra, it definitely was not meant to be presented as the objective facts of the setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am also quite open to the idea that traditional ideas held by the Garou about what is &quot;corrupt&quot; or &quot;unnatural&quot; could be incorrect; I enjoy the possibility, for example, that the Garou are misinterpreting the Wyrm as &quot;corrupt&quot; when it is actually functioning as intended, but that functioning is hostile to their own existence and they convince themselves it is unnatural and must be opposed as a result. As you say, things that are natural are not always nice or good for the things living in nature. And it is entirely possible that the Kindred condition, while dark and predatory, is not truly unnatural or corrupt; there are certainly plenty of Kindred who believe that as well.<br /> <br /> The truth of it actually does not matter, because the only point I was really trying to make is that Koldunism will certainly *appear* to be corrupt and unnatural to the Garou or other traditional shamans and animists; if they see their own practices reflected, it will be regarded as a degeneration at best, a perverse mockery of their beliefs at worst. They aren't going to look at a Koldun feeding his 'tainted' blood to the spirits of nature and think &quot;maybe I need to be more open-minded about how Leeches interact with the Umbra?&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the effect on the appearance and nature of the Penumbra, I certainly don't think the Umbra needs help being more dangerous. But what I am thinking is that the effect of it has an influence on the *flavour* of that danger. There are relationships between the Material and Spirit Worlds, and I feel like someone practicing spirit magics powered by supernatural blood sacrifice, that is going to have consequences over time. Nature is brutal, but it's brutal in many different ways; nature isn't always hungry for blood in a very literal sense. And to me it just kind of made sense that &quot;ghouling&quot; the local spirits as part of your magic would be inclined to make those spirits more vampiric. And since Vampires tend to ping Wyrm-sense regardless of whether or not they are actually of the Wyrm, it made sense that vampiric influence on spirits would do the same. Again, purely a personal extrapolation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4364_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4364\" data-vbnamecard=\"4364\">Orkar</a>'s question about unity among Koldun, the answer is probably &quot;as much as necessary, and not one bit more.&quot;<br /> <br /> Going back to the quote above that I took from &quot;Tome of Secrets,&quot; that was the lead-up to a mechanic they introduced where Koldun in the Dark Ages have to struggle against a supernatural compulsion to seek out any new Koldunic powers that they hear about, along with a risk of frenzying if they see another Koldun use a power they don't know. That's an extremely new mechanic, however, one which didn't exist for most of the history of Koldunic Sorcery as a Discipline.<br /> <br /> More generally, many Koldun are just like the stereotypical Tzimisce but <b>more</b>. By which I mean proud and territorial, but often bound by traditional codes of conduct, particularly pertaining to hospitality. I can't remember which book it was in, but the intro-fiction for one chapter involved the story of someone who was invited to visit a powerful Koldun, one who had been their enemy in the past. It was an excellent depiction of what it's like to encounter a skilled Koldun within their Domain (V20 Lore of the Clans, the introduction to the Tzimisce chapter).<br /> <br /> More generally, Tzimisce tend to feud with one another until forced to unite by outside circumstances, and even then they might continue to maneuver against one another in the hopes of coming out of the current struggle on top. Author fiat aside, it's one of the main reasons that the Tremere could survive going to war with the Tzimisce in the heart of their territory when they were barely out of their metaphorical diapers as vampires. They have enough pride as a Clan that they will tend to work together to avenge slights against the honour of the group, but they are not altruists or dependable allies as a rule. Even the codes of conduct that they follow around hospitality and such are about pragmatism as much as anything; you are a good host when a fellow Fiend needs it so that you know you can rely on another Fiend if you have to, and any Tzimisce who break those sacred rules can expect to be ostracized at best, or collectively destroyed at worst, only because that is the way the system keeps working for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 05-30-2023, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T13:45:12-07:00","id":1513319,"title":"","content":"story goes the wyrm went corrupt and instead of balancing the weaver went full force wanting to corrupt everything and i dont mean entropy to nothing, it seems to me the wyrm wants to spread suffering, disease, decay, deformation. Nephandi want to just end things, they are in this regard more entropic than the wyrm is and while the wyrm is still a part of existance, the nephandi want to undo even that, in special the wyrm.<br /> <br /> &quot;while dark and predatory, is not truly unnatural or corrupt&quot; - well they were cursed that sounds unnatural and corrupt to me ^^<br /> <br /> &quot;will certainly *appear* to be corrupt&quot; it stems from an earthbound demon that wants to end the world. so...as far as i understand it the spirits kolduns use are tainted, not the pure spirits of nature that shamans deal with. i could be wrong here but as far as i know the dreamspeakers and verbena view vampires as unnatural and tainted as well, they just dont mind that too much. just like wraiths arent the way they are supposed to be, but that doesnt mean they have to be destroyed.<br /> <br /> that would btw a good point to explore that further. Verbena do blood sacrifice, dreamspeakers with spirits, euthanatoi deal with death. How would they view a koldun and the spirits he commands? <br /> <br /> To cooperation - if Kolduns drink each others blood at Kuppalas Night...wouldnt they be blood bound to each other? at least 1 step","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T13:50:10-07:00","id":1513320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions#post1513165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont know maybe im reading this wrong but it sure seems like koldunism is pretty weak compared to other blood sorceries. Having regional restrictions, physical restrictions, affecting the caster, being more expensive and for that is being outright weaker on top with less diversity. Or am i just mistaken and dont grasp the true power of Kolduns, that id love to have explained to me XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is worthwhile to mention in regard to this that often there is the possibility and the chance for skill, priorities, style, wisdom, courage, and patiance of a Vampiress who is a Blood Magician can definitely count and matter more than for example wealth and variety of knowledge, definite power, or tested, certain, and impressive methods. <br /> <br /> Anothet option is to cooperate, or maybe become lovers, partners, or friends with another Blood Magician. There is also the possibility of becoming friends or allies with a Vampire ( or an Obertus Revenant, or a Grimaldi Revenant, or a Ventrue Ghoul ) who has the desire and ambition to become a Blood Magician, or some different type of spellcaster or wizard.<br /> <br /> This type of Blood Magic does seem to be more specialized than other types of Blood Magic. Thus it is normal and sensible to seek and create situations where specialized and particular castings, rituals, spells, and powers give distinct and unique gains,results, or advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T14:03:28-07:00","id":1513321,"title":"","content":"One of the most delightful things about the World of Darkness, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4364_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4364\" data-vbnamecard=\"4364\">Orkar</a>, is that it's overflowing with liars <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Even in the very rare instances where the authors come out and give you answers to the Big Questions, they will usually 1) push very hard that they are offering one interpretation and you are welcome to do your own thing instead, and 2) present several contradictory options.<br /> <br /> So for example, with Vampires, most of the material is going to push the Caine/Book of Nod message. But you're also going to have the Setites disagreeing. The Laibon also have some opinions they'd like to share. And that doesn't even consider that the Garou story about the Bloody Man may actually be the right answer.<br /> <br /> And then if we do settle, 100%, that we're going with the Noddist interpretation, which one? The modern &quot;Book of Nod&quot; and the &quot;Erciyes Fragments&quot; have a lot of differences between them, which is the accurate interpretation?<br /> <br /> Now, take all of those questions, and apply that level of skepticism to the generic background myths handed out to the Garou or to Mages. At the end of the day, none of them are ever more true than the Storyteller wants them to be; beyond making sure that the mechanics and the lore, the crunch and the fluff, line up with each other, the Storyteller can do pretty much whatever they want so long as everyone is having fun.<br /> <br /> So if it seems a little strange that some of us are pitching things completely at odds with what the books have said, it's because the books are intentionally unreliable at times <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, the Tzimisce claim that Koldunism is the oldest blood magic, and figuring out the specific order of many prehistoric events in the World of Darkness is rather tricky. So don't take the Baali's claim about doing it first at face value, especially since they're Baali :P<br /> <br /> <br /> To your specific question, you are correct that the ritual of Kupala's Night would create a level one Blood Bond, assuming the ritual doesn't neutralize that aspect of the vitae somehow (it may, or may not, I can't recall). I'd have to double-check how long it takes for lesser Blood Bonds to fade, but there's a good chance that performing the ritual once per year would not push the Bond past level one. And a level one Blood Bond simply isn't that powerful of a connection; it gives the regnant a bit of an alluring &quot;je ne sais quoi&quot; and that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T14:24:43-07:00","id":1513325,"title":"","content":"Our definitions of natural fundamentally clash, I think. Simply; existence and nature <i>are</i> the same to me, and the laws of science are often irrelevant to the WoD so the fact that vampires are functioning outside the laws of real world science doesn't matter. The WoD has other natural laws, and vampires fall within them.<br /> <br /> In reality, under our understanding of nature, a corpse can not walk around. If that did happen, that would not make it unnatural, it would mean our grasp of natural law and what is natural was incorrect and incomplete. And in the WoD, that is the case. <br /> Wyrm taint, vampires and nephandi and everything else is an expression of the nature of the world of darkness - which is twisted, suffering, insane and begging to die because the metaphysical cycle is broken and needs to reboot.<br /> <br /> No big deal if we don't get each other though.<br /> ---<br /> <br /> I think it's a difference in clan culture and paradigm that flavours it a bit differently for me.<br /> The Tremere are well behaved members of the Camarilla who should know better than to try raining Masquerade-breaching Armageddon on a city in the modern nights, with a very formulaic magic system. Kolduns are solitary, self-styled lords of the night who have dark, witchraft kinda vibes. Not sure how to word it, it's just... different to me.<br /> <br /> (And necromancy is perfectly cinematic, if you know what you're doing with the right arcanoi.\u200b)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-30-2023, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T15:44:30-07:00","id":1513337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513325#post1513325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our definitions of natural fundamentally clash, I think. Simply; existence and nature <i>are</i> the same to me, and the laws of science are often irrelevant to the WoD so the fact that vampires are functioning outside the laws of real world science doesn't matter. The WoD has other natural laws, and vampires fall within them.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>*A lone Mage in the distance rants about Paradigms to an empty sky in response to a conversation he didn't partake in and shouldn't know about*</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T21:10:56-07:00","id":1513356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513325#post1513325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our definitions of natural fundamentally clash, I think. Simply; existence and nature <i>are</i> the same to me, and the laws of science are often irrelevant to the WoD so the fact that vampires are functioning outside the laws of real world science doesn't matter. The WoD has other natural laws, and vampires fall within them.<br /> <br /> In reality, under our understanding of nature, a corpse can not walk around. If that did happen, that would not make it unnatural, it would mean our grasp of natural law and what is natural was incorrect and incomplete. And in the WoD, that is the case.<br /> Wyrm taint, vampires and nephandi and everything else is an expression of the nature of the world of darkness - which is twisted, suffering, insane and begging to die because the metaphysical cycle is broken and needs to reboot.<br /> <br /> No big deal if we don't get each other though.<br /> ---<br /> <br /> I think it's a difference in clan culture and paradigm that flavours it a bit differently for me.<br /> The Tremere are well behaved members of the Camarilla who should know better than to try raining Masquerade-breaching Armageddon on a city in the modern nights, with a very formulaic magic system. Kolduns are solitary, self-styled lords of the night who have dark, witchraft kinda vibes. Not sure how to word it, it's just... different to me.<br /> <br /> (And necromancy is perfectly cinematic, if you know what you're doing with the right arcanoi.\u200b)</div> </div> </div> </div>well i do get you i think, if for you nature and existance is the same then it logicly follows that everything that exists is natural, which makes vampires natural. I just think that most inhabitants of the world of darkness, which is based on our real world or better is our real world with supernatural elements added, would take &quot;our&quot; real world definition of natural - im pretty sure garou, mages and most humans would label vampires unnatural. I even think most of the kindred would do so as well as their very existance was brought upon by a curse as something that should not be.<br /> <br /> And yes i agree, Kolduns are more likely to go overboard, and as i understand it thaumaturgy, like the hermeticism the Tremere base it on, is a scientific rational formulaic approach to magic, while koldunism is more intuitive, shamanistic. Which is also shown in the rolls needed, as afaik thaumaturgy is a simple roll of willpower no matter the path, forcing your will onto the world, while each koldunic way uses a different attribute, stamina for way of earth, manipulation for way of fire and so on <br /> <br /> (which i might add is another &quot;weakness&quot; compared to thaumaturgy as a koldun that wants to master more than one way also has to upgrade more attributes than a thaumaturge)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T21:16:59-07:00","id":1513358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513321#post1513321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the most delightful things about the World of Darkness, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4364_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4364\" data-vbnamecard=\"4364\">Orkar</a>, is that it's overflowing with liars <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>XD well sure i agree there is little we can take for granted or to be sure and storytellers are encouraged to make of it whatever they please. But that doesnt mean there arent widely accepted interpretations like Saulot being evil is kinda confirmed across sources. just like there may be many many many possible origins of the Baali but given that all data we actually have on their founders is in agreement that all of them are fourth gen vampires, with nergal that is confirmed in werewolf the apocalypse books, which means all theories that make the Baali founders first or second generation vampires are wrong. I think in the case of there being 13 2nd gen Baali founders was even officially removed from canon (that was in the book of seker the red death and that was officially decanonised)<br /> <br /> similiarily that the unnamed baali founder is Lilith or Zillah or the crone is also kinda thrown out the window as all of them would be 2nd gen vampires, yet since all baali founders are the same generation and we know for sure moloch and nergal are fourth gen the unnamed must be someone else. You can change that as ST if you like, but that would be considered non canon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T08:29:12-07:00","id":1513398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513358#post1513358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> XD well sure i agree there is little we can take for granted or to be sure and storytellers are encouraged to make of it whatever they please. But that doesnt mean there arent widely accepted interpretations like Saulot being evil is kinda confirmed across sources. just like there may be many many many possible origins of the Baali but given that all data we actually have on their founders is in agreement that all of them are fourth gen vampires, with nergal that is confirmed in werewolf the apocalypse books, which means all theories that make the Baali founders first or second generation vampires are wrong. I think in the case of there being 13 2nd gen Baali founders was even officially removed from canon (that was in the book of seker the red death and that was officially decanonised)<br /> <br /> similiarily that the unnamed baali founder is Lilith or Zillah or the crone is also kinda thrown out the window as all of them would be 2nd gen vampires, yet since all baali founders are the same generation and we know for sure moloch and nergal are fourth gen the unnamed must be someone else. You can change that as ST if you like, but that would be considered non canon</div> </div> </div> </div>But, to use your first example, it isn't a &quot;widely accepted interpretation&quot; that Saulot is Evil. If you read &quot;Transylvania Chronicles,&quot; then Saulot is Evil. If you take the source material from the First Edition as your guide, then Saulot was Good. If you use &quot;Lair of the Hidden,&quot; then Saulot was at least Good-ish. I think if there was a &quot;widely accepted interpretation&quot; for Saulot, it would probably be that he is Complicated.<br /> <br /> If the source material itself is not going to be committed to any kind of consistent facts or truths of &quot;canon,&quot; then why should the players? The &quot;widely accepted interpretations&quot; are often just propaganda, history as written by the winners, etc. So to go back to your Baali example, you are correct that the interpretation of three Fourth Generation Baali Founders is probably the most widely accepted one. But I don't think that it's correct to say that &quot;all the data we have supports it.&quot; There are choices being made in that assessment, about which sources are to be trusted and which are regarded as lies. I think the only &quot;concrete&quot; data we get on the Baali Founders comes in the form of Nergal/Huitzilopochtli AFAIK, with everything else being rumour and legend, and there are plenty of possible alternatives to the 3-Founder-Baali interpretation that can drawn simply from a lying Fourth Generation.<br /> <br /> And when nearly all of the details around the Ancients is explicitly and intentionally kept obscured, there is no good reason to place any special value or weight on an interpretation simply because it is the most popular. In fact, there are some popular interpretations that I actively oppose, because I think they make the story less interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T17:45:50-07:00","id":1513903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513398#post1513398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But, to use your first example, it isn't a &quot;widely accepted interpretation&quot; that Saulot is Evil. If you read &quot;Transylvania Chronicles,&quot; then Saulot is Evil. If you take the source material from the First Edition as your guide, then Saulot was Good. If you use &quot;Lair of the Hidden,&quot; then Saulot was at least Good-ish. I think if there was a &quot;widely accepted interpretation&quot; for Saulot, it would probably be that he is Complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is before getting into the possible canon that there are Two saulot's thanks to some weirdness after a vacation in the east.<br /> <br /> Honestly I like saulot for this specific reason, they Are complicated. Something with 10,000+ years of life Should be nuanced and complicated enough that their motivations could fill the Iliad and the Odyssey combined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T19:05:02-07:00","id":1513906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1513903#post1513903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is before getting into the possible canon that there are Two saulot's thanks to some weirdness after a vacation in the east.<br /> <br /> Honestly I like saulot for this specific reason, they Are complicated. Something with 10,000+ years of life Should be nuanced and complicated enough that their motivations could fill the Iliad and the Odyssey combined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two Saulots is my favourite theory, currently <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do want to acknowledge that I feel like I've contributed to the thread being derailed a bit, albeit unintentionally. And I am a huge fan of Koldunism, so I'd love to discuss that more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T17:58:10-07:00","id":1514529,"title":"","content":"To bring back to Koldunism, the other upside I see for it is that Thaumaturgy is something that you can only really be taught by others, and even if you know one Path, it\u2019s not necessarily a given that you have the sources to learn another, and replicating them via experimentation to \u201cself teach\u201d is incredibly risky. <br /> <br /> Koldunism, on the other hand, is deals with nature spirits. If you have access to a water source, and the Occult skill to communicate with the Water Spirit as a Koldun, you can bargain with it to use the Way of Water. To then learn the Way of Earth, you don\u2019t need to find a willing teacher or books etc like Thaumaturgy, you just need an Earth Spirit. <br /> <br /> Once you know \u201cKoldunism\u201d, learning Ways is just a matter of what spirits you have bargains with. Knowing the Path of Blood doesn\u2019t guarantee being able to learn the Path of Technomancy, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T21:53:31-07:00","id":1514547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1514529#post1514529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To bring back to Koldunism, the other upside I see for it is that Thaumaturgy is something that you can only really be taught by others, and even if you know one Path, it\u2019s not necessarily a given that you have the sources to learn another, and replicating them via experimentation to \u201cself teach\u201d is incredibly risky.<br /> <br /> Koldunism, on the other hand, is deals with nature spirits. If you have access to a water source, and the Occult skill to communicate with the Water Spirit as a Koldun, you can bargain with it to use the Way of Water. To then learn the Way of Earth, you don\u2019t need to find a willing teacher or books etc like Thaumaturgy, you just need an Earth Spirit.<br /> <br /> Once you know \u201cKoldunism\u201d, learning Ways is just a matter of what spirits you have bargains with. Knowing the Path of Blood doesn\u2019t guarantee being able to learn the Path of Technomancy, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting point for sure! However, I'd argue that &quot;self-teaching&quot; in Koldunism is no less risky than doing the same with Thaumaturgy; the dangers are different, but they exist. A Koldun that simply attempted to work things out on their own without relying on pre-existing traditions would essentially be going into their dealings with the spirit-world blind; spirits can be unpredictable, and potentially dangerous. While Thaumaturgy certainly comes with many risks, they don't necessarily require the involvement of a second party that is going to bring its own agenda to the table.<br /> <br /> One of the unfortunate blind spots that comes from Vampire dealing fast-and-loose in most of its engagement with Otherworld content is that there is very little material detailing the particular relationships between Koldun, spirits, and the Umbra. AFAIK there isn't a lot of firm mechanics regarding the connections between Koldun and the spirit-world beyond the effects of rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:37:09-07:00","id":1514609,"title":"","content":"Did we ever get an answer on how the split between the kraina and the paths happened? Is it a roads-to-path-o'-enlitenment scenario where the kraina were the fleshed out version that got lost in the inquisition and hastily reconstucted or are the paths a kind of &quot;Americanized&quot; diet kraina much like the local food?<br /> <br /> An interesting note: the Old Kraina seem more &quot;Spiritual&quot; than demonic with how they seem more like expressions of nature and how the old rites function like werecreature Gifts. Modern Paths seem to lean more &quot;Demonic&quot; in how it closely mirrors Thaumaturgy(which is diet infernalism in it's own right) and how it's paths are closer to the elemental power of the fallen in DtF than natural forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 06-11-2023, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T16:34:23-07:00","id":1514633,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always headcanoned it as the main Clan lost access to the Kraina on Kupalas Night where not only did they break their blood bonds, but also metaphysically tied themselves to Kupala, so all Koldunism is now performed through that lens. Old Clan, and those that they and their ancestors have avoided Vaulderie, could still have access to the \u201cpure\u201d Kraina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T07:50:33-07:00","id":1515536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1514609#post1514609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we ever get an answer on how the split between the kraina and the paths happened? Is it a roads-to-path-o'-enlitenment scenario where the kraina were the fleshed out version that got lost in the inquisition and hastily reconstucted or are the paths a kind of &quot;Americanized&quot; diet kraina much like the local food?<br /> <br /> An interesting note: the Old Kraina seem more &quot;Spiritual&quot; than demonic with how they seem more like expressions of nature and how the old rites function like werecreature Gifts. Modern Paths seem to lean more &quot;Demonic&quot; in how it closely mirrors Thaumaturgy(which is diet infernalism in it's own right) and how it's paths are closer to the elemental power of the fallen in DtF than natural forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hardly canon, but for my TC game where I landed on the transition from old form Koldunism to Koldunic Sorcery, was Kupala's binding in 1314. Very long story short, Kupala's binding severed the ancient ties and pacts that allowed old form Koldunism to function, but newer practitioners figured out how to brute force it without reliance on chiminage.<br /> <br /> That it vaguely resembles Tremere Thaumaturgy is no coincidence: Vykos was one of the pioneers of Koldunic Sorcery. Vykos was a mortal mage; specifically, a Hermetic of House Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T09:05:10-07:00","id":1515750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1515536#post1515536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's hardly canon, but for my TC game where I landed on the transition from old form Koldunism to Koldunic Sorcery, was Kupala's binding in 1314. Very long story short, Kupala's binding severed the ancient ties and pacts that allowed old form Koldunism to function, but newer practitioners figured out how to brute force it without reliance on chiminage.<br /> <br /> That it vaguely resembles Tremere Thaumaturgy is no coincidence: Vykos was one of the pioneers of Koldunic Sorcery. Vykos was a mortal mage; specifically, a Hermetic of House Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vykos is typically depicted in their stat spreads as using Thaumaturgy; did your version use Koldunic Sorcery instead, or were they involved with the development while still using Thaumaturgy themselves? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T16:34:42-07:00","id":1515798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1515750#post1515750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vykos is typically depicted in their stat spreads as using Thaumaturgy; did your version use Koldunic Sorcery instead, or were they involved with the development while still using Thaumaturgy themselves? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not something I can really answer; my TC game was heavily house-ruled, and I changed NPC stats quite a bit. Vykos was by far the one whose stat block changes were the most drastic. But most importantly, I house ruled the various styles of blood sorcery as a rough analog to paradigm from Mage to prevent characters from having multiple sorcery disciplines; under those rules Vykos had Ways, but as secondary Thaumaturgy paths.<br /> <br /> But had I done things RAW, I would have given Vykos dots in both Koldunic Sorcery and Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T09:15:09-07:00","id":1515872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513165-koldunism-questions?p=1515798#post1515798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not something I can really answer; my TC game was heavily house-ruled, and I changed NPC stats quite a bit. Vykos was by far the one whose stat block changes were the most drastic. But most importantly, I house ruled the various styles of blood sorcery as a rough analog to paradigm from Mage to prevent characters from having multiple sorcery disciplines; under those rules Vykos had Ways, but as secondary Thaumaturgy paths.<br /> <br /> But had I done things RAW, I would have given Vykos dots in both Koldunic Sorcery and Thaumaturgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>At first I was going to say that I was looking for your house-ruled response, but then I realized you meant that things had changed so much that the question-as-posed didn't quite work any more, haha. Very neat, thanks for explaining <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do feel like there was at least one edition of Blood Magic rules that supported the idea of buying Paths/Ways outside of your &quot;Paradigm&quot; for additional XP cost.<br /> <br /> But as someone who also likes drawing the connections between Vampire and Mage, as well as Sorcery and Magic, I can see what you mean about how it's strange that &quot;Paradigms&quot; for Vampires are treated as their own Discipline, separate from Paths, while Sorcery Paths are just self-contained, with no central &quot;core Power&quot; like Thaumaturgy/Koldunism/etc., even though different Paths can presumably be used in multiple &quot;Paradigms.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}